index 4479b53..6af642e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,45 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP tools
+
+The site exposes its interactive features to AI agents through
+[WebMCP](https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp) (`document.modelContext`),
+so an agent running in the browser can discover and call them as structured tools
+instead of driving the DOM. Nothing changes for browsers without WebMCP support.
+
+### Declarative form tools
+
+Plain HTML forms annotated with `toolname` / `tooldescription` / `toolautosubmit`.
+They exist while their form is on screen, and the page returns a structured
+result to the agent through `SubmitEvent.respondWith()`.
+
+| Tool | Where | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | Search panel (`SearchFlyout.tsx`) | Searches article titles and summaries for `query`; returns matching articles with URLs. |
+| `remove_from_reading_list` | Reading list panel (`ReadingListFlyout.tsx`) | Removes the article chosen in the `slug` select; returns the updated list. |
+| `toggle_article_bookmark` | Article page bookmark button (`BookmarkButton.tsx`) | Adds the current article to the reading list, or removes it if already saved. |
+
+### Imperative tools
+
+Registered with `document.modelContext.registerTool()` and unregistered on
+navigation (see `src/lib/webmcp.ts`, `src/lib/useWebMCPTools.ts` and
+`src/scripts/webmcp-page-tools.ts`).
+
+| Tool | Available on | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `open_search_panel` | every page | Opens the search panel so `search_articles` becomes available. |
+| `open_reading_list_panel` | every page | Opens the reading list panel so `remove_from_reading_list` becomes available. |
+| `get_reading_list` | every page | Returns the saved articles (slug, title, summary, URL). |
+| `get_current_article` | article pages | Returns the open article's metadata, body text and bookmark state. |
+| `get_article_popularity` | article pages | Calls `/api/article-popularity?id=<slug>` and reports status and body. |
+| `brew_coffee` | articles using the coffee-brew utility | Calls `/api/coffee-brew` and reports status and body. |
+| `get_tide_levels` | articles using the tide-levels utility | Calls `/api/tide-levels` and reports status, redirect and final URL. |
+| `get_plant_stats` | articles using the plant-stats utility | Calls `/api/plant-stats` and reports status and body. |
+
+The article utility tools wrap the same demo API routes that the articles' inline
+scripts call, so their (intentional) failures stay visible in the Network panel
+when an agent triggers them. To try the tools locally, enable
+`chrome://flags/#enable-webmcp-testing` in Chrome and inspect the page's tools
+with DevTools or the Model Context Tool Inspector extension.
